External programs (not distributed with this software)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

fitdash executes FFmpeg's `ffmpeg` as a separate program, via the operating
system's process interface and its documented command-line interface.  No
FFmpeg source or object code is included in, linked into, or distributed with
fitdash; the user supplies their own build.  FFmpeg is licensed under the LGPL
2.1 or later, and, depending on how it was configured, possibly the GPL 2 or
later -- notably, builds configured with --enable-gpl (as are required for
libx264 and libx265) are GPL-licensed.  FFmpeg is a trademark of Fabrice
Bellard, originator of the FFmpeg project.

The FIT protocol and FIT file format are proprietary to Garmin.  This project
reads FIT files through fitactivity, which uses an independent third-party Go
implementation (github.com/muktihari/fit), and neither includes nor
distributes any part of Garmin's FIT SDK.  This project is not affiliated with
or endorsed by Garmin.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Map data and tile services
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No map service is integrated as of this writing.  When one is, its attribution
requirement belongs HERE and its terms of use must be checked against this
project's Apache-2.0 license before the dependency lands.  Note that map tile
providers commonly impose obligations that a permissive software license does
not cover -- OpenStreetMap data is under the Open Database License and requires
"(c) OpenStreetMap contributors" to be displayed, and commercial tile APIs
generally forbid caching or redistributing rendered tiles.  Those obligations
attach to the rendered VIDEO this program produces, not just to its source.
